// sourceIPFlightTimeout is the per-request deadline for one shared lookup.
//
// The external-IP check is a courtesy lookup for one status field, and it must
// never be the reason an operation waits: an endpoint that accepts the connection
// and then stalls — which is what an unreachable resolver looks like — used to
// hold the caller for as long as the socket stayed open, so a run sat in
// `running` with no error. The bound is per request, overridable through
// RR_SOURCE_IP_LOOKUP_TIMEOUT_MS, and it never shortens a value the operator
// supplied.
//
// It lives here, on the flight, because the flight is what performs the request.
// The deadline belongs to the one request that is actually open — a caller that
// merely waited on someone else's answer is already bounded by that same request.
func sourceIPFlightTimeout(ctx context.Context) (context.Context, context.CancelFunc) {
	return context.WithTimeout(ctx, sourceIPLookupTimeout())
}

